  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe estate tax rate under the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion (TRAIN) law is a flat rate of 6% on the value of the estate exceeding Five Million Pesos (₱5,000,000).\n\n### Interpretation\nSection 84 of the NIRC specifies that the estate tax is computed based on the net estate of the deceased, which is the gross estate less allowable deductions. The flat rate of 6% applies only to the portion of the estate that exceeds the threshold of ₱5,000,000.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, this means that estates valued at ₱5,000,000 or less are exempt from estate tax. For estates valued above this threshold, only the amount exceeding ₱5,000,000 will be taxed at the 6% rate. This simplification aims to ease the tax burden on smaller estates while ensuring that larger estates contribute fairly to government revenues.",
